@node Running tests
@section Running tests

The package includes a comprehensive ERT test suite in @samp{pdf-tools-pages-test.el}. Because @samp{pdf-tools} requires a compiled C server that cannot run in headless CI environments, all @samp{pdf-tools} functions are mocked with @code{cl-letf}. The tests cover page selection, DWIM toggling, qpdf argument construction, exit code handling, buffer-local isolation, and the extract/delete workflows.

To run the tests locally:

@example
make test
@end example

To byte-compile:

@example
make compile
@end example

Both targets expect @samp{pdf-tools} to be available as a sibling directory (@samp{../pdf-tools/lisp}), which is the case for elpaca-managed installations.

@node Continuous integration
@section Continuous integration

A GitHub Actions workflow runs byte-compilation and the full test suite on every push and pull request to the @samp{main} branch. Tests are run against Emacs 27.1, 29.4, and 30.1 to ensure broad compatibility.

